  "scope": "Reduce repeated startup kernel measurements in paper validation; no changes to image objectives, geometry, paper tolerances, deadlines or acceptance thresholds.",
  "policy": "Compare JavaScript and WebAssembly outputs on each of the first two actual requests in a size bucket, in opposite orders. Return the current JavaScript result during calibration. Enable WebAssembly only after both outputs match and both paired timings show a greater than 10% gain. Retain timings only. Other measured-kernel clients keep their previous default policy.",
  "integration": "Enabled locally through paperBackend at c484669. Prototype opted in at its two materialAudit call sites; the production wrapper supplies the same option. Generic default remains false. Focused integrated tests passed, but full inverse QA failed (880/895); native corpus and browser stages did not start. Follow-up isolates a frozen-clock test contamination and an overly restrictive intermediate-routing assertion; eight corrected tests pass. Remaining failures are unresolved. See paper-calibration-release-failures.json.",
